yer 2.5)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2.5-1. R&D Capitalisation [Estimate]:\n  R&D \u2248 18% of revenue FY25 (~$530M). 3-year amortisation \u2248 $400M.\n  Adjusted OI \u2248 $646M + $530M \u2212 $400M \u2248 $776M (vs GAAP $646M).\nStep 2.5-2. SBC Adjustment [Actual]:\n  FY25 SBC = $146M. True FCF = GAAP OCF \u2212 SBC \u2212 full capex.\n  FY25 true FCF (pack OCF $717M \u2212 SBC $146M \u2212 $94M capex) = $477M.\n  This is the correct cash-generation baseline: 16.2% FCF margin.\nStep 2.5-3. Operating Leases [Actual]:\n  Operating leases $0.089B. Adjusted net debt = \u2212$0.33B. Immaterial.\nStep 2.5-4. Data Asset [Estimate]:\n  Cloud data across 5,000+ enterprise CX deployments is valuable for\n  AI training; monetisation via CXAI ARR $362M, +52% YoY [Actual].\n  I do NOT add a separate data-asset valuation to the DCF \u2014 it is\n  embedded in growth forecasts.\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC [Estimate]:\n  GAAP ROIC ~13.6%; R&D-expanded ROIC ~15.0%. Gap < 5pp \u2192 within\n  normal range. No red flags.\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett) [Estimate]:\n  FY25: NI $612M + D&A $199M \u2212 maintenance capex $50M \u2212 \u0394WC $50M\n  (normalised) \u2212 SBC $146M = $565M. (Raw \u0394WC \u2212$539M is distorted by\n  Actimize-sale prep and HMRC ramp; normalised \u0394WC used.)\n\nSECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (Layer 3 \u2014 Engine 1 + SOTP)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u