c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2524\n  \u2502  9.0%        \u2502  $167  \u2502  $178  \u2502  $192  \u2502\n  \u2502 10.0%        \u2502  $143  \u2502  $153  \u2502  $165  \u2502\n  \u2502 11.0%        \u2502  $126  \u2502  $134  \u2502  $144  \u2502\n  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n  Top-3 sensitivity variables (Thesis KPIs): (1) Cloud revenue growth\n  after FY26; (2) True FCF margin / SBC level; (3) Actimize sale price\n  and closing probability.\n\nREVERSE DCF / MARKET IMPLIED EXPECTATIONS:\n  At $100.24, market cap = $5,858M.\n  Less net cash ($328M); less Actimize at only 50% probability and\n  $2.0B after-tax ($1,000M) \u21d2 implied continuing EV = $4,530M.\n  At 10% WACC/3% terminal: implied FCF = $317M on $2.64B revenue \u21d2\n  12.0% FCF margin AND 0% terminal growth.\n  \u21d2 The market is pricing ZERO long-term growth and a 12% FCF margin,\n  i.e. it is assuming AI disruption kills CCaaS and pricing concessions\n  erode cash generation permanently.\n\nMULTIPLES CROSS-CHECK:\n  Forward P/E: 9.0\u00d7 on FY26 non-GAAP EPS $11.16 [Actual \u2014 guidance].\n  EV/EBITDA: ~9\u00d7 [Estimate \u2014 research brief].\n  5-yr average: ~30\u00d7 P/E, ~27\u00d7 EV/EBITDA [Estimate \u2014 research brief].\n  Trailing GAAP P/E: 14.49\u00d7 [Actual \u2014 pack].\n  Even at 12\u00d7 FY26 non-GAAP EPS (a mature software multiple), the stock\n  is worth $134 (+34%). At 15\u00d7, $167 (+67%).\n\nTORNADO RANKING:\n  1. Cloud growth post-FY26 (\u22123pp to +5pp): \u2212$25 / +$40 per share.\n  2. True FCF margin (\u22122pp to +3pp): \u2212$18 / +$27 per share.\n  3. Actimize sale outcome ($1.5B to $3.0B): \u2212$13 / +$17 per share.\n  4. WACC (+1pp/\u22121pp): \u2212$19 / +$25 per share.\n  5. Terminal growth (\u22120.5pp/+0.5pp): \u2212$10 / +$12 per share.\n\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n1. Competitive response: If NICE's AI/outcome pricing succeeds, Zoom,\n   Genesys, Five9, and Microsoft will respond with aggressive AI-native\n   pricing. Impact on NICE: \u22122 (moderately negative). This is already\n   visible in Q2 pricing concessions.\n2. Reflexivity (Soros): Negative feedback loop currently active \u2014\n   depressed share price weakens SBC attractiveness, risks talent flight\n   to AI-native startups, and raises CEO-transition friction. Positive\n   loop triggers if the stock recovers to $130+: $2.5B Actimize proceeds\n   enable buybacks (shares \u22126% YoY already), M&A currency improves, and\n   partner/customer confidence strengthens.\n3. Customer evolution: Early-adopter AI customers (tech-forward\n   enterprises) are now signing; mainstream customers will take 2\u20134\n   years. AI bookings (+72% backlog) do not convert linearly. NRR of\n   106% reflects concessions to lock multiyear AI deals \u2014 a deliberate\n   investment in LTV.\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (Layer 4 \u2014 Bayesian)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25